.TH ACCOUNT-AUDIT 1 "October 2026" "SASD Freeware" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
account-audit \- read-only structural audit of a Unix passwd file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B account-audit
.RB [ --file " PATH]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Examines seven-field Unix-style passwd records for invalid fields,
duplicate usernames, shared UIDs, additional UID-0 accounts and empty
shells. Legacy NIS compatibility entries are skipped with warnings.
Does not change user accounts or read shadow passwords.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --file " PATH"
Input file (default /etc/passwd).
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Show usage.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 if no malformed entries (warnings may exist), 1 for malformed
entries, 2 for bad usage, and nonzero on input failures.
.SH EXAMPLE
.B account-audit --file /etc/passwd
.SH NOTES
Does not inspect PAM, LDAP/NSS, shadow passwords, or password quality.
The output can disclose account names. Shared UIDs are not always errors.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR passwd (5),
.BR getent (1)
